#. Forward-declared functions
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:71
msgid "Dimitri?"
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:71
msgid ""
"Dimitri should be around here, but you can't see him. You should probably "
"look for him."
msgstr ""

#. Creates the mission
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:82
msgid ""
"You enter the bar, but you can't seem to find Lt. Commander Dimitri. As you "
"look around for him, you feel a heavy hand fall on your shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. Adds escorts
#. Handles arrival back to base
#. Just landing
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:83
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:339
#: dat/missions/minerva/finale2.lua:790
msgid "Guard A"
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:84
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:340
#: dat/missions/minerva/finale2.lua:791
msgid "Guard B"
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:86
msgid ""
"It seems like two armed soldiers are here to escort you somewhere, and from "
"the looks of their weapons, they mean business. You have no choice other "
"then to comply."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:87
msgid ""
"They start leading you away from the bar through some hallways you've never "
"been through before. Must be all those 'Authorised Personnel Only' signs and "
"the armed guards that didn't make them too appealing."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:89
msgid ""
"Finally they toss you into what seems to be an interrogation room, simply "
"telling you to wait. After what seems to be a whole period, you hear the "
"door open."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:90
msgid "Door Guard A"
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:91
msgid "Door Guard B"
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:95
msgid ""
"You see a highly decorated woman walk in, with two soldiers standing guard "
"at the door. She seems to be a Commodore, from the insignia on her uniform."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:96
msgid ""
"\"Hello. I'm Commodore Keer. I've taken over the Collective issue. I have "
"heard about your success in the previous missions and would like to offer "
"you more work. However, further proceedings must be kept in strict "
"confidentiality for the interest of the Empire.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:97
msgid "\"Are you willing to go all the way with this?\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:108
msgid ""
"You accept and she dismisses both of the soldiers, who proceed to wait "
"outside."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:109
msgid ""
"\"We've been following Lt. Commander Dimitri's progress since he started at "
"{pnt}. The datapad you brought back has confirmed what we have suspected: we "
"have an undercover Collective agent somewhere in the military who's been "
"feeding ex-Commodore Welsh data. You don't understand, right? Let me explain."
"\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:110
msgid ""
"\"The Collective was actually a project for the Empire. They were supposed "
"to be the ultimate weapon in flexibility and offense. Commodore Welsh was in "
"charge of the secret science facility on {pnt}. Shortly after the Incident, "
"we stopped hearing from them. We sent a recon and were met with hostile "
"Collective drones.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:111
msgid ""
"\"It seems like the project had been a success, but the traitor, Welsh, went "
"rogue. Under normal circumstances we would have easily crushed the "
"Collective, but after the Incident, these are hardly normal circumstances.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:112
msgid ""
"She goes on. \"Things have gotten out of hand. We have had chances to crush "
"Welsh, but he always seems to evade us and strike where we are weakest. We "
"always knew there must have been another traitor in our midst, but with the "
"datapad information we now know who he is.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:113
msgid ""
"Commodore Keer has taken over the Collective issue and explained more about "
"the Collective. \"The Collective was actually a project for the Empire. They "
"were supposed to be the ultimate weapon in flexibility and offense. "
"Commodore Welsh was in charge of the secret science facility on {pnt}. "
"Shortly after the Incident, we stopped hearing from them. We sent a recon "
"and were met with hostile Collective drones. It seems like the project had "
"been a success, but the traitor Welsh went rogue. Under normal circumstances "
"we would have easily crushed the Collective, but after the Incident, these "
"are hardly normal circumstances.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:114
msgid ""
"She now clears her throat. \"This operation has been dubbed 'Operation Black "
"Trinity'. We have reason to believe that the ESS Trinity has been operating "
"with the traitor Welsh. The ESS Trinity is commanded by Captain Zakred. You "
"will form part of an assault team with the primary objective of arresting "
"Zakred. As a last resort, you are authorized to kill Zakred. He must not "
"escape.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec05.lua:115
msgid ""
"\"We'll be sending you with a small force. We expect you to hang back, but, "
"if any trouble arises, take the ESS Trinity down. Zakred is currently on "
"manoeuvre exercises in {sys}. You will have to find him there. The other "
"ships will follow your lead to {sys}. Good luck.\""
msgstr ""

