#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:308
msgid ""
"As you approach to land on {pnt}, you notice big banners placed on the "
"exterior of the station. They seem to be in celebration of the final defeat "
"of the Collective. Upon landing, you are saluted by the welcoming committee "
"in charge of honouring all the returning pilots."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:310
msgid ""
"You notice Commodore Keer. Upon greeting her, she says, \"You did a good job "
"out there. No need to worry about the Collective any more. Without Welsh, "
"the Collective won't stand a chance, since they aren't truly autonomous. "
"Right now we have some ships cleaning up the last of the Collective; "
"shouldn't take too long to be back to normal.\""
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:311
msgid ""
"She continues. \"As a symbol of appreciation, you should find a substantial "
"deposit in your account. There will be a celebration later today in the "
"officer's room, if you want to join in.\""
msgstr ""

#. This was the last mission in the minor campaign, so bump the reputation cap.
#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:322
msgid "And so ends the Collective threat..."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:323
msgid ""
"You don't remember much of the after party, but you wake up groggily in your "
"ship clutching an Empire officer's boot."
msgstr ""

#: dat/missions/empire/collective/ec06.lua:333
msgid ""
"You helped the Empire to finally destroy the Collective once and for all. "
"The Collective is now no more."
msgstr ""

